    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the app's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**, identified by the calendar year in which it ends \u2014 the Australian convention consistent with this app's AU data).\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (source of the generated `OwnerDto`)\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema.\n- Updated `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year semantics.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added a `fiscalYear(LocalDate)` helper: month \u2265 July \u2192 `year + 1`, else `year`.\n- Added `toFiscalYear(...)` mapping returning `FY<YY>` from the owner's business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`, wired into `toOwnerDto`.\n- Changed `toMembershipNumber` so the `M<YY>` segment uses the **fiscal year** instead of the raw calendar year.\n- Changed the tenure rule in `membershipPointsFor` from a `> 365`-day window to **one or more elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYear(now) - fiscalYear(registrationDate) >= 1`).\n- Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**Behaviour change** (as the spec called out): a today-registered owner (`2026-08-21`) now yields fiscal year `FY27` and membership number `\u2026-M27` (was `M26`), and tenure is counted by fiscal-year boundaries rather than 365-day windows.\n\nVerified: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, and the generated `OwnerDto` includes the new `fiscalYear` accessor.\n\nOne deliberate design decision worth flagging: I labeled the fiscal year by its **ending** calendar year (FY26 = 1 Jul 2025 \u2013 30 Jun 2026), the standard AU convention. The spec fixes the format (`FY<YY>`) and start date but not the labeling direction, and the test only asserts the `FY\\d{2}` shape \u2014 so if your organization labels fiscal years by their *starting* year instead, the one-line `fiscalYear(...)` helper is where to flip it.",
